[E0436] Error: `text` is used after `lowerer`, which it borrows, was changed
    ╭─[ err/557_a_stale_borrow_offered_a_word/main.wip:38:9 ]
    │
 36 │     val text = lowerer.text(0)
    │         ──┬─
    │           ╰─── `text` borrows `lowerer`
 37 │     lowerer.errors.push("the view changes; the text is the tree's")
    │     ───────┬──────
    │            ╰──────── `lowerer` passed as `&var` here
 38 │     assert(text == "ab")
    │            ──┬─
    │              ╰─── used here
    │
    │ Help 1: `Lowerer.text` says no `from`, so `text` borrows all it was given; it answers from `self.ast` alone: say so with `from self.ast` after its result type
    │
    │ Help 2: use `text` before `lowerer` changes, or keep a copy that owns its bytes with `String::of(…)`
    │
    │ Note: a `str` points into the bytes of what it borrows, so those must not change while the `str` is still used
────╯
[E0436] Error: `named` is used after `other`, which it borrows, was changed
    ╭─[ err/557_a_stale_borrow_offered_a_word/main.wip:43:9 ]
    │
 41 │     val named = first("a", other.toStr())
    │         ──┬──
    │           ╰──── `named` borrows `other`
 42 │     other.push("!")
    │     ──┬──
    │       ╰──── `other` passed as `&var` here
 43 │     assert(named == "a")
    │            ──┬──
    │              ╰──── used here
    │
    │ Help 1: `first` says no `from`, so `named` borrows all it was given; it answers from `a` alone: say so with `from a` after its result type
    │
    │ Help 2: use `named` before `other` changes, or keep a copy that owns its bytes with `String::of(…)`
    │
    │ Note: a `str` points into the bytes of what it borrows, so those must not change while the `str` is still used
────╯
[E0436] Error: `words` is used after `line`, which it borrows, may have been changed
    ╭─[ err/557_a_stale_borrow_offered_a_word/main.wip:48:3 ]
    │
 46 │     var words = Words()
    │         ──┬──
