 48 │         words.clear()
    │         ──┬──
    │           ╰──── used here
    │
 50 │         line.push(text)
    │         ──┬─
    │           ╰─── `line` passed as `&var` here
    │
    │ Help 1: `Words.clear` leaves `words` holding nothing it held: say so with `empties`, after its signature
    │
    │ Help 2: use `words` before `line` changes, or keep a value that owns its data
    │
    │ Note: a view points into what it borrows — a `str` into bytes, a `&` into a place — so that must not change while the view is still used
